    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
    "english": "The Yellow River is China's second-longest river, about 5,464 kilometres in all. It rises in Qinghai province, flows through nine provinces and regions, and empties into the Bohai Sea in Shandong. Because its middle reaches cross the Loess Plateau, the river carries more silt than any other in the world and looks yellow. As the cradle of Chinese civilisation it is honoured as the 'mother river', though historically it also flooded many times.",
