    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
    "english": "The Mid-Autumn Festival falls on the 15th day of the 8th lunar month, when the moon is at its fullest. It is an important traditional festival of family reunion: people go home, share mooncakes and admire the bright moon together. The round mooncakes symbolise reunion and completeness. Today the festival is celebrated wherever Chinese people live, and the streets are full of mooncake gift boxes before the festival arrives.",
