    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
    "english": "Peking opera took shape in 19th-century Beijing by merging Anhui opera with Han tunes and absorbing the strengths of other arts. Performers tell stories through song, recitation, acting and acrobatic fighting. The painted faces use bright colours to show each character's personality — red for loyalty, white for cunning. honoured as a national treasure, Peking opera joined UNESCO's intangible heritage list in 2010.",
