    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
    "english": "Hotpot is a special way of eating: a pot of boiling soup is set in the middle of the table, and diners cook slices of meat, vegetables, tofu and noodles in it themselves and eat them straight away, so the food is always hot. The most famous style is the numbing-and-spicy Sichuan hotpot, while northerners prefer the light mutton hotpot. In winter, sitting around a steaming pot with family and friends is warm and happy, which is why hotpot is loved all over China.",
